(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The full C API's layouts (queue 269; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 269\"; 262's DECISION (a), the user"] [4 1 "// 2026-11-10, and 268's DECISION (a), 2026-11-11). Without Py_LIMITED_API, CPython 3.14.10's Include/ reads objects in"] [5 1 "// place: Py_TYPE(o)->tp_flags (PyTuple_Check and the other subclass checks), PyList_Type.tp_new, PyTuple_GET_ITEM's"] [6 1 "// ob_item, PyList_GET_ITEM's ob_item array, PyBytes_AS_STRING's ob_sval, PyFloat_AS_DOUBLE's ob_fval. So:"] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "//   - a type's handle is a PyTypeObject (PyHeapTypeObject's 936 bytes, or the world's static struct of a type"] [9 1 "//     Include/ names) filled as CPython's: tp_name, the sizes, tp_flags, tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, and its"] [10 1 "//     function slots (a type made from a spec its C functions, a pyi type the natives of the generic protocol);"] [11 1 "//   - a tuple's, list's, bytes' and float's handle is a mirror: the object's CPython layout in the world's memory,"] [12 1 "//     made when C first sees the object and kept in step with the pyi value at the C boundary, both ways (as PyPy's"] [13 1 "//     cpyext does): from Go to C before the world is called and when a native returns (the objects it touched), from"] [14 1 "//     C to Go when the world returns and when a native receives a mirrored object (its first use in the native). A"] [15 1 "//     container's mirror holds references to its items' handles, as CPython's container holds its items: a slot C"] [16 1 "//     writes (PyTuple_SET_ITEM, PyList_SET_ITEM) steals the reference C gave, a slot Go changes holds a new one and"] [17 1 "//     gives the old one back, and a mirror released gives its items back."] [18 1 "//"] [19 1 "// Layouts from Include/cpython/{object,tupleobject,listobject,bytesobject,floatobject}.h (CPython 3.14.10, LP64; the"] [20 1 "// PSF's license, LICENSE.md); the slots' offsets are Objects/typeslots.inc's."] [36 1 "// PyTypeObjec