itten back to C when it returns."] [741 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [753 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [755 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [756 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [757 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [758 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [759 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [760 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [768 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [781 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [784 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [790 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [802 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [803 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [820 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [821 1 "// a new reference."] [848 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [849 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base's own value, or for an"] [850 1 "// exception the exception of sub itself."] [870 1 "// bornWith makes the instance of sub keeping the built-in value v (for an exception, v is the instance), its memory"] [871 1 "// the world's: tp_basicsize bytes (and nitems items') or the mirror's size, the built-in part mirrored."] [920 1 "// allocObj is tp_alloc's generic allocation of t (PyType_GenericAlloc): a C-born object, an instance over a built-in"] [921 1 "// base, or a type object's memory (type's own tp_alloc: a heap type C fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [924 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [945 3 "// a built-in type of pyi's whose zero value is an instance (queue 594: _io._BytesIOBuffer's tp_alloc in"] [946 3 "// test_pep3118_obsolete_write_locks): a new reference"] [958 1 "// rawTypes are the type objects C allocated through type's tp_alloc, not ready yet."] [961 1 "// bornDealloc is a built-in base's tp_dealloc on a C instance's memory (list_dealloc, tupledealloc ...): its items'"] [962 1 "// references given back as CPython's do, read from its memory, the list's array and the memory freed."] [984 1 "// ---- PyType_Ready for a type object of C's memory (a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc) ----"] [986 1 "// typeReady is PyType_Ready (Objects/typeobject.c, type_ready) of the type object at a: a pyi type made from its"] [987 1 "// fields (NewExtType), its slots the C functions it names and those it inherits, its handle a; the fields"] [988 1 "// PyType_Ready fills written back (tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, the inherited slots, Py_TPFLAGS_READY)."] [1007 37 "// type_ready_set_new's tp_new before inheritance"] [1015 2 "// the base and the bases"] [1078 39 "// type_ready_set_new: a static type over object without tp_new"] [1080 2 "// inherit_slots: a C base's, else the generic natives of a pyi base"] [1094 3 "// inherit_slots (queue 270b): tp_vectorcall_offset, Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_VECTORCALL when tp_call is inherited (a"] [1095 3 "// static type is immutable), Py_TPFLAGS_METHOD_DESCRIPTOR when tp_desc