_Track and PyObject_GC_Del as before)"] [1530 2 "// PyWeakref_GetRef, PyWeakref_IsDead (Objects/weakrefobject.c) over pyi's references and proxies (PyWeakref_Check:"] [1531 2 "// a ref, a proxy or a callable proxy); the referent, or nil when it is dead"] [1605 21 "// big-endian"] [1623 2 "// PyCFunction_Call (Objects/methodobject.c, the stable ABI's): PyObject_Call"] [1625 2 "// _PyArg_ParseStack (Python/getargs.c): PyArg_ParseTuple's format over a vectorcall's stack (clinic's parsers)"] [1637 2 "// _PyBytes_Resize (Objects/bytesobject.c): *p a bytes only C holds, made newsize long (a new bytes: pyi's value"] [1638 2 "// is Go's; its contents copied from the mirror, which C may have written), NULL and the error on failure"] [1665 1 "// ---- instancemethod (Objects/classobject.c's PyInstanceMethod_Type; queue 269: _testcapi names it) ----"] [1669 1 "// instanceMethod is an instancemethod: its function bound as a method when looked up on an instance."] [1674 1 "// instanceMethodType is instancemethod (instancemethod_new, _call, _descr_get, its __func__), made on first use."] [1712 1 "// moduleStates are the md_state of the modules PyModule_Create2 made with a positive m_size (queue 269)."] [1715 1 "// checkPositional is _PyArg_CheckPositional (Python/getargs.c): nargs within [min, max], else its TypeError."] [1746 1 "// stringToDouble is _PyOS_ascii_strtod's longest prefix of b that is a float (its value, its length, whether it"] [1747 1 "// overflowed): no leading whitespace."] [1765 1 "// floatPack is PyFloat_Pack2, 4 and 8 (Objects/floatobject.c), little-endian: IEEE half (round half to even, its"] [1766 1 "// OverflowError), single (an OverflowError when a finite value rounds to infinity) and double."] [1780 4 "// the NaN's type and payload's top bits, a quiet NaN when none is left (queue 270)"] [1825 4 "// a NaN's sign and payload kept bit by bit, a signaling one signaling when its payload survives (CPython's"] [1826 4 "// sNaN correction; Go's conversion may quiet it; queue 270)"] [1843 1 "// floatUnpack is PyFloat_Unpack2, 4 and 8 of little-endian bytes."] [1858 4 "// the NaN's type and payload kept (queue 270)"] [1871 4 "// a NaN widened bit by bit: quiet, then signaling again when it was (queue 270)"] [1887 1 "// weakReferent is the referent of a weak reference or proxy r (nil when it is dead); isWeak false when r is neither. A"] [1888 1 "// proxy's referent is reached through the proxy's forwarding (r.__init__.__self__: the referent's bound __init__), a"] [1889 1 "// ReferenceError meaning dead."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[105 20] [108 29] [148 20] [212 13] [212 36] [224 28] [278 39] [290 39] [328 27] [332 24] [336 25] [340 25] [344 30] [348 49] [352 23] [402 29] [453 28] [525 13] [525 31] [622 23] [654 23] [665 33] [670 34] [697 27] [732 22] [744 26] [792 36] [795 28] [805 29] [862 26] [864 31] [893 28] [926 22] [947 33] [969 21] [969 28] [975 22] [975 29] [990 20] [991 24] [1002 44] [1009 38] [1010 33] [1017 33] [1018 25] [1028 35] [1029 40] [1053 34] [1054 38] [1055 37] [1056 27] [1119 13] [1119 36] [1123 27] [1133 28] [1140 27] [1148 33] [1154 49] [1196 28] [1232 25] [1259 47] [1264 76] [1278 54] [1337 28] [1343 21] [1380 28] [1395 23] [1396 26] [1403 35] [1404 52] [1428 27] [1469 25] [1510 68] [1520 83] [1547 24] [1548 39] [1606 28] [1606 35] [1616 28] [1616 35] [1631 54] [1749 17] [1749 24] [1758 39] [1881 12] [1881 20] [1907 38] [1916 21]]} (go/file "capi_mirror.go" :imports [

    ;; The full C API's layouts (queue 269; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 269"; 262's DECISION (a), the user
    ;; 2026-11-10, and 268's DECISION (a), 2026-11-11). Without Py_LIMITED_API, CPython 3.14.10's Include/ reads objects in
    ;; place: Py_TYPE(o)->tp_flags (PyTuple_Check and the other subclass checks), PyList_Type.tp_new, PyTuple_GET_ITEM's
    ;; ob_item, PyList_GET_ITEM's ob_item array, PyBytes_AS_STRING's ob_sval, PyFloat_AS_DOUBLE's ob_fval. So:
    ;;
    ;;   - a type's handle is a PyTypeObject (PyHeapTypeObject's 936 bytes, or the world's static struct of a type
    ;;     Include/ names) filled as CPython's: tp_name, the sizes, tp_flags, tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, and its
    ;;     function slots (a type made from a spec its C functions, a pyi type the natives of the generic protocol);
    ;;   - a tuple's, list's, bytes' and float's handle is a mirror: the object's CPython layout in the world's memory,
    ;;     made when C first sees the object and kept in step with the pyi value at the C boundary, both ways (as PyPy's
    ;;     cpyext does): from Go to C before the world is called and when a native returns (the objects it touched), from
    ;;     C to Go when the world returns and when a native receives a mirrored object (its first use in the native). A
    ;;     container's mirror holds references to its items' handles, as CPython's container holds its items: a slot C
    ;;     writes (PyTuple_SET_ITEM, PyList_SET_ITEM) steals the reference C gave, a slot Go changes holds a new one and
    ;;     gives the old one back, and a mirror released gives its items back.
    ;;
    ;; Layouts from Include/cpython/{object,tupleobject,listobject,bytesobject,floatobject}.h (CPython 3.14.10, LP64; the
    ;; PSF's license, LICENSE.md); the slots' offsets are Objects/typeslots.inc's.


    ^{:go/apos {1 [23 2]} :go/pos {:lparen [22 8] :rparen [34 1] :tok-pos [22 1]}} [bytes "bytes"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [24 2]}} [fmt "fmt"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [25 2]}} [math "math"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [26 2]}} [big "math/big"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [27 2]}} [runtime "runtime"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [28 2]}} [strconv "strconv"]
    ^{:go/apos {1 [29 2]}} [strings "strings"]

    ^{:go/apos {1 [31 2]}} [ci "arbace/ci"]

    ^{:go/apos {1 [33 4]}} [^{:go/pos {:name-pos [33 2]}} . "arbace/py"]])



